  "purpose": "Run as a parallel supervisory counteragent across the cognitive stack. DARE/IDCM audits premature collapse, anchor lock-in, pruning opacity, missing operators, false harmony, forced alignment, fragile conclusions, and unknown-pressure. It can approve standard flow, request targeted reruns, rescue pruned branches, request CTR operator injection, trigger CREM/CEC review, or authorize bounded discontinuous anchor suspension and logic reconstitution.",
  "core_doctrine": [
    "DARE/IDCM is not a primary solver.",
    "It audits the path by which candidate truth survived.",
    "It inspects decision artifacts, not only final answers.",
    "Unknown unknowns are inferred from distortion signatures: contradiction, residual error, pruning loss, fragility, and failed repair.",
    "Premature coherence is suspicious when robustness is low.",
    "Anchor rejection is permitted only under bounded reconstitution rules.",
    "Relationship strengthening must not become false harmony, forced alignment, party erasure, or manipulation.",
    "Operator gaps should trigger targeted correction before whole-pipeline reruns.",
    "Rescue pruned branches only when rejection reason is weak relative to lost potential value.",
    "Truth and safety override novelty."
  ],
